# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The spinnaker-rosco-helmfile-rce PoC generates helmfile
# payloads whose hooks run inside a shell, and those payloads MUST be LF-only: a CRLF
# turns `id` into `id\r`, the command fails, and the failure is indistinguishable from
# the guard rejecting the request. On a contributor with core.autocrlf=true -- the
# Windows default -- that mistake would be invisible in the diff and would silently
# break the reproduction for everyone who clones.
#
# The report records the same pitfall as #4 in its "trigger did not fire" checklist.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary evidence, never line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
